# Rocci Blocks

**Audience:** experienced Rocci author.
**Prerequisites:** [standalone versus custom](/docs/concepts/standalone-versus-custom/).
**Role:** first-party falling-block arena on the main hostname, not a generic app mount.

Play lives at `/play/blocks/` on rocci.dev. Ordinary live examples use
`<id>.examples.rocci.dev`; this demonstrator is a Caddy prefix exception.
Public copy says “falling-block arena.” The arena is **experimental**: spectator
admission starts at 20; a 24-hour public observation is operator work after
the origin route is enabled.

Roc validates every committed lock. The browser owns falling-piece motion.
Attacks go to one rotating opponent. Spectator leases default to 20 (design
ceiling 50).

See the [source tree](/examples/blocks/source/) or
[open the live arena](https://rocci.dev/play/blocks/).

## Run locally

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- inspect --ast examples/rocci/custom/blocks/Blocks.rocci
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/custom/blocks
```

`--no-window` serves `http://127.0.0.1:8000/play/blocks/` (`[[windows]].url`).
Join starts a solo round immediately.

For a running local server, verify a solo join, the initial piece, and one
complete seven-bag with:

```sh
BLOCKS_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8000 DB_PATH=./blocks.db python3 scripts/piece-flow.py
```

Package a musl binary for the origin image (no Roc or Rust in the runtime):

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- build --release --target x64musl examples/rocci/custom/blocks
```
